---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.governance;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="container prose-card">
    <p class="section-kicker">Proposed public stewardship</p>
    <h2>A public standard needs accountable decisions</h2>
    <p>TENSOR's intended specification, essential public profiles, schemas, and basic conformance materials should be accessible without buying a product or sponsorship. Vendor participation is welcome; funding must not purchase control over shared meaning.</p>
    <p><strong>The governance proposal is not yet adopted.</strong> It does not appoint a council, create a legal entity, grant new intellectual-property rights, or establish institutional backing. Repository access alone is not independent oversight.</p>
    <p><a href="/founding/02-governance.md">Download the complete governance proposal</a> · <a href="/founding/00-charter.md">Read the founding charter</a></p>

    <h2>Accepted bootstrap stewardship</h2>
    <p>On October 11, 2026, John Schieferle Uhlenbrock accepted bootstrap stewardship under the TENSOR Standards Consortium project identity, including the three operational roles below. These responsibilities currently concentrate in one founder; independent oversight is not established. <a href="/docs/stewardship.md">Read the dated record, disclosure status and pending account confirmations</a>.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Responsibility</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Convenor</td><td>Reviews, decisions, appeals, and scope.</td><td>John Schieferle Uhlenbrock</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Core editor</td><td>Consistent semantics and specification text.</td><td>John Schieferle Uhlenbrock</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Conformance maintainer</td><td>Fixtures, validation coverage, and implementation evidence.</td><td>John Schieferle Uhlenbrock</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Profile editors</td><td>Domain content and source quality.</td><td>Unassigned in the proposal</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Independent reviewers</td><td>Practitioner, research, and implementation challenge.</td><td>Open participation</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Contact and feedback</h2>
    <p>The bootstrap convenor coordinates public <a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/issues/new?template=implementation-report.yml">technical findings</a> and <a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/issues/new?template=core-rfc.yml">process proposals or escalation</a>. Sensitive reports use <a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/security/advisories/new">private vulnerability reporting</a>. No staffed service or independent appeal body is claimed.</p>
    <p><a href="/docs/review-process.md">Finding and dissent handling</a> · <a href="/review/">Frozen technical review</a></p>

    <h2>Proposed decision process</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Publish a numbered proposal with the problem, examples, alternatives, compatibility effects, and acceptance evidence.</li>
      <li>Allow at least 14 days for technical review and 30 days for breaking, charter, or governance changes.</li>
      <li>Record substantive objections and their disposition. Material revisions restart review.</li>
      <li>Publish the decision, rationale, reviewers, conflicts, and unresolved issues.</li>
      <li>Archive approved text, schemas, fixtures, and migration guidance together.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Before a first stable release, the proposal requires substantive assessments from at least two reviewers independent of the principal authors and each other. A later five-person council is a proposed transition, not a claim of current representation.</p>

    <h2>Participation without privileged status</h2>
    <p>Disclose affiliations and conflicts. Keep funding conditions visible. Record dissent and appeals. Use synthetic or authorized de-identified cases. Existing licenses remain applicable to existing materials; contribution, patent, and stewardship policies need explicit review before adoption.</p>
    <p><a href="/contribute/">Contribute a review or implementation</a> · <a href="/founding/05-review-plan.md">Review the evidence gates</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
